Engineering Summary: Ephemeral Zero-Trust Compute Agent1. Architectural OverviewDesigned and implemented an autonomous, stateless execution agent capable of dynamic cloud-native bootstrapping, bare-metal hardware profiling, and secure ephemeral processing. The architecture enforces strict zero-trust principles by ensuring zero local persistence upon task completion.2. Key Technical CapabilitiesDynamic Cloud Ingestion: Automated runtime environment hydration, pulling necessary assets from secure cloud storage into an isolated, temporary working directory on demand.Autonomous Hardware Interrogation: Real-time host introspection via system management interfaces to evaluate available compute silicon (CPU/GPU acceleration tiers) and bind execution pathways dynamically without pre-configured driver assumptions.Cryptographic & Tensor Execution: Native execution of modular lattice math and matrix-vector forward-pass transformations (modeled over prime rings such as $Z_{65537}$) to validate computational integrity and throughput.Self-Annihilating Lifecycle Management: Automated zero-trace cleanup routines that purge all transient sandbox artifacts, clear runtime memory caches, and restore secure directory navigation upon task completion.3. Impact & Use CasesProvides a highly portable, secure execution cell suitable for confidential computing environments, automated edge-node diagnostics, and immutable task processing where forensic footprints must be strictly avoided.
